\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. I will not let Thee go, Thou help in the time of need:
\par Heep ill on ill,
\par I trust Thee still,
\par Even when it seems that Thou wouldst slay indeed.
\par Do as Thou wilt with me,
\par I yet will cling to Thee;
\par Hide Thou Thy face, yet: Help in time of need,
\par I will not let Thee go!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. I will not let Thee go. Should I forsake my bliss?
\par No, Thou art mine,
\par And I am Thine;
\par Thee will I hold when all things else I miss.
\par Though dark and sad the night,
\par Joy cometh with Thy light,
\par O Thou my Sun: Should I forsake my bliss?
\par I will not let Thee go!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. I will not let Thee go, my God, my
\par Life, my Lord:
\par Not death can tear
\par Me from His care,
\par Who for my sake His soul in death outpoured.
\par Thou diedst for love to me;
\par I say in love to Thee,
\par Even when my heart shall break,my God, my Life, my Lord,
\par I will not let Thee go!
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

